Z||000000||Chris Ward||01-22-2001||05:08 PM||||My egr tube has a leak and i took it off and put a plate over to hole in the intake. Do you need this tube? and if so why?<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||01-22-2001||05:22 PM||||Nah, you don't need it. GM just put it there for S&G <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||01-22-2001||05:29 PM||||Yes, it is very important. It keeps the engine from detonation and self destructing. It adds exhaust gasses back into the cylinders to help cool the engine.it lowers the oxides of nitrogen (NOX) gasses.<P>Ogre you can probably elaborate on this.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||Tom Philips||01-23-2001||07:48 AM||||The egr tube should be connected The exhaust gas is used as a dilutent to lower emissions also when the egr valve is active it also advances spark .. so if you have egr plugged you will be prone to more spark knock and higher emissions||||reg||1
